"notes": ["Source: 2026 Philadelphia Eagles Media Guide, RECORD BOOK (pdf pp. 207-262). PDF page numbers are used; the page footers print only the guide name, no page numbers. Lists used: PASSING pp. 212-214, RUSHING pp. 217-219, RECEIVING pp. 222-224, SACKS p230, INTERCEPTIONS pp. 234-235. Each category has a Career page, a Season page and a Game page; the big yards/receptions tables (top 20) and separate boxes for touchdowns, receiving yards and sacks exist, so every list here is ranked by exactly its stat (kind=list for all 27 present pairs).","through_season 2025: the lists carry 2025 entries (Dallas Goedert (2025) 11 receiving TDs on p223, Saquon Barkley (2025) in the season rushing table on p218, Brandon Graham (2010-25) in the career sacks box on p230, A.J. Brown (2022-25) on pp. 222-223) and the guide is the 2026 edition dated 2026-08-13.","Ties: the guide prints the rank on the first row of a tie group ('5t.') and leaves it blank on the following tied rows; those rows here carry the shared rank with tie=true. 'raw' keeps the printed text without a rank for such continuation rows.","Names: positional tags such as (QB), (TE), (RB), (E), (FL), (WR/K), (DE) and the year span are printed after the name; the name field has only the name, the tag stays in raw, years holds the span as printed (for example '2008-13, '19-20' for a two-stint career, '2020-' for a player still active in 2026). Rows of players still active with the club are printed in bold in the guide (for example Jalen Hurts (2020-)).","Game lists: the guide prints dates as M/D/YY; years holds M/D/YYYY (YY 33-99 read as 19YY, YY 00-25 as 20YY, safe because the club began in 1933); the printed opponent stays in raw. Opponent names are as printed (Yanks, Reds, Boston Yanks, Chi. Cardinals, StL Cardinals, L.A. Raiders).","The rushing-yards game list (p219) contains two postseason games: rank 6 Steve Van Buren 12/18/49 at Rams and rank 7 Wilbert Montgomery 1/11/81 vs. Cowboys, both shown as playoff games (NFL-C, NFC-C) in the guide's PLAYOFF RECORDS p255. No other game list row appears in the playoff pages (pp. 254-256 checked for passing, rushing, receiving, sacks and interceptions).","Game receiving TDs: only two single-game rows are printed (4 TDs); the third printed line is the aggregate '24x, last: A.J. Brown (10/30/22 vs. Steelers)' and was left out.","Sacks: the only qualifier is the note under the career table, 'Only includes figures since 1982 (when sacks became an official NFL statistic)'; the season and game boxes have no note of their own.","Big tables (career passing/rushing/receiving yards, career receptions, season rushing yards, season receiving yards) print 20 or 25 rows; only the top 10 rows were transcribed and complete_to says how many the guide prints. Every transcribed row was compared with the page picture (110 dpi page views; digits double-checked on crops), and the printed Pct, Y/A and Avg columns were recomputed from the transcribed attempts, completions, yards and carries as an arithmetic cross-check (no mismatches).","Tackles: no list in any scope (see 'missing')."]
